{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01456",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.23,
      "end_seconds": 6.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Actually, hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.42,
      "end_seconds": 12.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 15.26,
      "end_seconds": 22.15,
      "duration_seconds": 6.89,
      "text": "Doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.78,
      "end_seconds": 25.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.15,
      "end_seconds": 40.38,
      "duration_seconds": 13.23,
      "text": "I wanted to get a tight band around my head looked at. I'm not great at remembering details, you know, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.29,
      "end_seconds": 44.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "So, what's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.2,
      "end_seconds": 61.65,
      "duration_seconds": 15.45,
      "text": "About... well, ten days. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.99,
      "end_seconds": 71.82,
      "duration_seconds": 9.83,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.64,
      "end_seconds": 112.81,
      "duration_seconds": 39.17,
      "text": "I'd call it mild. I notice it more with stress. It just comes and goes. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. I've had a stiff neck too, for one week. As for stiff neck, moderate, really. Honestly, a couple of times a week. Oh, you know, and tired eyes. That's been about the same, about three months. Oh, uh, as for tired eyes, pretty severe, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.78,
      "end_seconds": 115.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Nothing like weakness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.18,
      "end_seconds": 121.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Yeah, no, I haven't had any weakness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.3,
      "end_seconds": 131.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any sensitivity to light or blurred vision?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.05,
      "end_seconds": 137.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Let me think, no, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.47,
      "end_seconds": 141.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "And sickness, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.76,
      "end_seconds": 145.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "No, none, no sickness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 146.43,
      "end_seconds": 152.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice sickness. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.15,
      "end_seconds": 164.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.97,
      "text": "Um, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.94,
      "end_seconds": 173.87,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.46,
      "end_seconds": 179.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, uh, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.25,
      "end_seconds": 182.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.35,
      "end_seconds": 185.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.66,
      "end_seconds": 189.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.54,
      "end_seconds": 196.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "My uncle has high cholesterol. My aunt has rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.63,
      "end_seconds": 200.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.06,
      "end_seconds": 208.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "Mm, I had two stents put in my heart three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.32,
      "end_seconds": 214.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.85,
      "end_seconds": 227.31,
      "duration_seconds": 11.46,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.31,
      "end_seconds": 242.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.39,
      "end_seconds": 245.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Yes, high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.06,
      "end_seconds": 247.76,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.31,
      "end_seconds": 257.63,
      "duration_seconds": 8.32,
      "text": "I mean, I have high blood pressure, for two years. I have heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.01,
      "end_seconds": 262.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Alright, have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.45,
      "end_seconds": 266.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.14,
      "end_seconds": 270.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.0,
      "end_seconds": 279.68,
      "duration_seconds": 7.68,
      "text": "Simvastatin. I take it 20 milligrams, at night. It's metoprolol, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.75,
      "end_seconds": 284.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.0,
      "end_seconds": 303.29,
      "duration_seconds": 17.29,
      "text": "50 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box. I take paracetamol, 1 gram, when needed. Sorry, uh, what was I saying, before this I was on clopidogrel; that's been stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.34,
      "end_seconds": 321.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.73,
      "end_seconds": 335.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.14,
      "end_seconds": 357.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 121 over 69, temperature 36.8, heart rate 65."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.49,
      "end_seconds": 360.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.82,
      "end_seconds": 365.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.46,
      "end_seconds": 371.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.23,
      "end_seconds": 373.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.24,
      "end_seconds": 387.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Your neck and shoulder muscles are tight, and your eye movements are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.99,
      "end_seconds": 395.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 412.89,
      "end_seconds": 437.09,
      "duration_seconds": 24.2,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: It's hard to say. Tension-type headache is one possibility and eye strain another, and I'd rather not commit yet. I'll request an eye test, it'll help with eye strain. Take screen breaks every hour and try regular neck stretches. Let's plan a check in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 437.66,
      "end_seconds": 439.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Okay, I'll arrange it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 440.52,
      "end_seconds": 443.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 444.74,
      "end_seconds": 446.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}